docs/api/** linguist-generated=true
*.sh text eol=lf

# Key-material fixtures (issue #238 cross-impl tests). `.keys.wrap` is raw
# random bytes small enough that git's own binary-content heuristic (which
# most .wasm/.enc blobs trip automatically via embedded NUL bytes) isn't
# reliable — a 32-byte random buffer has a good chance of containing zero
# NUL bytes. `keys.enc` is base64 text today (no embedded CR/LF to corrupt
# in its current committed content), but its exact bytes are just as
# load-bearing for the cross-implementation test, and a future regeneration
# could reintroduce a trailing newline or other text-normalization-sensitive
# byte. Without `-text` on both, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf
# enabled could rewrite bytes and break the cross-implementation test.
**/.keys.wrap -text
**/keys.enc -text
